      "text": [
        " : سَأَلَ سَعِيدٌ اَلْأَعْرَجُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ وَ أَنَا عِنْدَهُ عَنِ اَلْخَمِيصَةِ سَدَاهَا إِبْرِيسَمٌ وَ لَحْمَتُهَا مِرْعِزَّى فَقَالَ «لاَ بَأْسَ بِأَنْ تُحْرِمَ فِيهَا إِنَّمَا يُكْرَهُ اَلْخَالِصُ مِنْهَا »."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2611 - It was narrated from Abu al-Hasan al-Nahdi, who said:\nSa'id al-A'raj asked Abu Abdullah (as) in my presence about a garment (khamiṣah) whose warp was made of silk (ibrīsīm) and its weft was made of goat wool (mir‘izzā).\nImam (as) said: \"There is no harm in entering Ihram in it. What is disliked is the garment made entirely of silk.\""
        ]
      }
